{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the documentation follow-up at head dfe69293cf5aa6aa3c8e9a17156e29aa4d58f2cc, tree 445b8faf, for request c31315a1 and review request 95445da7. Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED, for three small wording repairs.\n\nI read section 6 of the review record first, then the diff from 4436d508 with main's changes set aside, against the 14 items of review 4f2e8b24. Twelve items hold. Item 14 and one sentence on a security page do not, and one repair in item 4 left a new mismatch.\n\n## Changes requested\n\n1. `docs/security/settings.md:97-98` gives the wrong default.\n   - The page says that `PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS` adds earlier pins \"besides the newest publication and unpublished families\".\n   - `packages/scope/src/creation-versions.ts:10` builds the default from three cohorts: `ARCHIVE_DEVICE_PUBLICATION_COHORT`, `UNPUBLISHED_COHORT` and `COMMONS_COHORT`. `docs/deploy.md` at this head names all three.\n   - A reader of the security page would conclude that an unset policy refuses Commons pins. It accepts them.\n   - Fix: name the three cohorts, as `deploy.md` does.\n\n2. Section 6 says that `cohort` is the one name, and that doesn't hold yet. These lines still use \"family\" for a cohort:\n   - `docs/write-an-application.md:115`, `:363-367` and `:407`;\n   - `docs/self-host.md:165`;\n   - `docs/security/settings.md:98-99`;\n   - `docs/security/trust-boundaries.md:78` and `:90`.\n\n   `docs/manual/ten-terms.md:103` also keeps \"when the room is claimed\", beside the line that this head changed to \"when the room is created\". Other uses of \"family\" mean something else and should stay: route families in `entry-points.md`, the tool family in `kernel.md`, the form families in `lanes.md` and the households in `use-cases.md`.\n\n3. `docs/what-is-dap.md:149` says that the page \"describes both paths\". The list above it now has three ways in. Name the paths that `apps/room/docs/page.md` describes.\n\n## Items of the first review\n\n1. `run