e holds main's text at line 1550. The one sentence that left the page is \"Review must assess these boundaries\", a duty of BO1's review, which has happened.\n- The footers match section 2. Eleven pages name c8c7b631, and they are the eleven that section 2 lists.\n\n## The merge of main\n\nI took every added line in `docs/`, `README.md` and `apps/room/docs` from 5dc9765f to c8c7b631, and looked for it at this head. The 69 lines that differ are rewordings, or process detail such as who reports what, and I read them in place:\n\n- `deploy.md`'s Commons section keeps its order and its limits, in operator wording.\n- `settings.md`, `entry-points.md` and `trust-boundaries.md` keep the `unplanned` closure and the separate boundaries.\n- The lines in `mcp.md` and `use-cases.md` keep their meaning.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main c8c7b631 gives the head tree 445b8faf. The head is 38 paths from main, all documents, and the 38 artifacts match that count.\n- From checkpoint d9b7ebdf to the head, only the record and the manifest change.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 969 links, 0 broken. check-commit-messages: 5 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check`: clean. `check-kernel-boundary`: 126 sources, 0 refusals.\n- check-notes gives one warning, on the relocated-text note, which section 2 expects.\n- I ran `security-entry-points.test.mjs` (10 of 10) and `security-settings.test.mjs` (3 of 3). The worktree stayed clean. Both pass with the sentence in item 1, so they don't guard it.\n- The evidence verifies. The manifest has SHA-256 4fe43d13. All 16 listed files match by size and SHA-256, `SHA256SUMS` reruns clean, and no file is unlisted or writable. Its logs show 40 of 40 for the MCP documentation tests and 4 of 4 for the lane definitions. I did not repeat those two.\n- The gate did not run, and the documents-only rule allows that: only documents differ from main.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe reading journey and the single-file decisions hold, and the deploy rules are back with the reader. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\nEvery duty from the first review is restored in plain terms. Item 1 misstates what an unset creation policy accepts. Changes requested, item 1.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe rewrite stays shorter and clearer than base. Item 2 finishes the one-name decision. Approved, with item 2.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: changes requested, item 1.\n- Simplification: approved, with item 2.\n- The request's checks: twelve of the 14 items hold in full, the merge lost no rule, and the evidence and tests hold. Items 1 to 3 remain.\n\nA head that makes these changes can come back for a review of its diff from this head. It changes only documents, so the documents-only rule applies again, and `security-settings.test.mjs` should run again.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:444a0556eb09ccc059f9db5f25cee62d168fac2b","binding":"assigned","head":"dfe69293cf5aa6aa3c8e9a17156e29aa4d58f2cc","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e954aadb6e199c596266e07f9c5c13f69fde3468\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:547c0c7f376a47d7ed48158feab9ebc7c6f79fec\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bdf11579925ae3f045796a3bfab3a8b045b25c2e","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}